//! #7609: jq never compiles the arguments of a call it cannot resolve (#2037), but the sites in them
//! are still sites of the source, so an undefined name named there and again later is cited at the
//! later site, as jq cites it: `def d0: ua(ub(1));` then `ub(2)` reports `ub/1` at the `ub(2)` of line
//! 2. The count skipped those arguments, so the error named the earlier site: an unused def's
//! (#3085 counted its body, not the arguments of an unresolved call in it), a hidden closure's, or
//! the main program's own (`ua(ub(1)),` then `ub(2)`). The wording of each error is #2703's and is
//! unchanged; what the rows pin is which line is cited and echoed.
//!
//! Every expectation was captured from jq 1.7.1 (`/usr/bin/jq`) over a generated matrix: the outer
//! unresolved call in ten shapes, five kinds of inner site (a call, a call of no arguments, a
//! variable, a `break`, a call inside a call), in five places. jq 1.8.2 cites the same sites; it
//! adds a column and a caret to the text (jqlang/jq#3292, a change to the message not adopted).

use anyhow::Result;

use crate::run_jq_full;

/// `(program, jq's stderr, exit status)`.
type Row = (&'static str, &'static str, i32);

